{"c":[{"id":"26929d8f3644a207","sum":"P2: page Asks return AskGoal.page, planned by goals/page-planner.ts; only lowering marks gate 'fill' (by identity), so GoalRuns.propose refuses a cloned plan. Headless CfT calls Google hosts anyway; oracle.ts files them under browserService().","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T220819Z-d4c70d849120ef71","text":"P2: an Ask about a page (goals:true) comes back as AskGoal.page and is planned by goals/page-planner.ts with no writer; its steps are gate 'fill', which only lowering marks (gates.ts markFilled, by identity), so GoalRuns.propose refuses a structuredClone'd page plan.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T224055Z-4008dd64a8214ebf","text":"Headless Chrome for Testing keeps calling Google hosts (google.com, googleapis.com) through a proxy whatever flags it gets; the F1 network sink (fixtures/web-form/oracle.ts) files them under browserService(), not offsite().","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1b95871ffb8fdb66","sum":"F1 probe posts drop after a burst, so the oracle can lag the DOM; page-loop-eval reads undo over CDP. 'from my notes' makes code read only the one window it resolves (planner/sources.ts); page-loop goal runs ask 'fill out this form' (whole form).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T005116Z-802d1a3e98c70699","text":"F1's probe posts state with fetch keepalive and drops a failed post after recording it sent, so after a burst of writes the oracle can lag the DOM; page-loop-eval checks undo by reading the DOM over CDP (DOM_VALUES_JS).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T005116Z-d31529fbf9335d38","text":"P2 evals: an Ask saying 'from my notes' makes code read only the one window it resolves that to (planner/sources.ts); on the corpus that was a decoy note. Page-loop goal runs ask 'fill out this form', which heads settles as a whole form.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
